        rules: {
          objective: 'Score 100+ points (Standard) or fulfill a special contract.',
          gameplay: '1. Must follow suit.\n2. If void, MUST play a trump card.\n3. **Must Overtake**: You must play a card higher than the current winning card if you have it.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit. If void in led suit, must play a trump.',
            'Must overtake: play a card higher than the current winning card when possible (even if partner is winning).',
            'Declarer plays alone against the two defenders, who form a team.',
            "Contracts (Suit, Betl, Durch, Open Betl, Open Durch) are chosen by bidding; forehand must name a contract, others say 'good' or 'bad' to take over.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "In a Standard game, focus on 'killing' the opponent's Aces and Tens. Use your trumps to seize the lead when you are void in a suit, then lead your own Ten to force them to play their King or Queen into your pile.",
          intermediate: "The Seven Management: If you bid 'Seven', you must keep the 7 of Trumps until the very last turn. This means you need enough other trumps to defend yourself throughout the round so you aren't forced to play the 7 early.",
          advanced: 'Defensive Coordination: In the 2-vs-1 setup, the defenders must work together. If your partner is leading a suit, and you have the Ten, play it! You are giving points to the partnership rather than letting the declarer take them later.',
          tips: [
            'Count the trumps. There are 8 in total. If you have 5 and your opponents play 2, only one remains. You are now the master of the table.',
            "In 'Betl', discard your highest cards (Ace, Ten) as soon as possible into suits where you are void.",
          ],
